comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-28T09:06:02.097Z","harness:codex","Live branch-policy evidence 2026-09-28: main has 26 strict required checks, linear history, and disabled force pushes/deletions, but enforce_admins=false and no branch rulesets. A ruleset/least-privilege policy migration must preserve the release push behavior delivered by pm-9gxi: the current Auto Release workflow still uses its maintainer release credential for the checked version commit and tag. Do not toggle administrator enforcement alone and break scheduled publication. Acceptance for the chosen policy approach should explicitly document or narrow the remaining administrator bypass while retaining required deterministic checks and proving a production release path. This is a governance follow-up, not evidence of a leaked credential or a new scanner finding."
